 they're  making gains the ukrainians are saying  that they've repelled attacks on Bahamut  from several angles on that City but  what I can tell you is that we were  there yesterday and we had to leave  because the Rockets were going over our  heads and we were forced to leave that  City now I was also there back in May  and the situation since May has  definitely changed there's more  destruction in the city there's fewer  people many people have left and where  we had gone to in the city before back  in may we can no longer reach that area  because the Russians are way closer now  the battle does change sometimes the  ukrainians say that they've pushed the  Russians further out the Russians  claiming that they're getting closer and  closer to that City but what I can tell  you is that yesterday that there was a  lot of firing going on lots of shells  being fired Rockets been fired lots of  Destruction fewer people there but right  now that City remains in the hands of  the ukrainians but the Russians are  making a push for it they're putting  considerable effort into taking  just not far away from what they're also  trying to take that strategic location  because if they manage to take those two  places it gives them a bit of a  strategic Advantage here in the East but  so far the ukrainians are saying that  they're holding on to it but definitely  I would say that the Russians are way  closer to Bahamut than they were back in  May all right thanks so much assadbag  well let's talk to Al jazeera's Muhammad  jamjun he's live in the Ukrainian  Capital where there have been large  power Cuts so what does life feel like  there on this Friday with all the power  cuts  well Sammy it's a very interesting  atmosphere here in Kiev let me first  walk you through what's happened over  the course of the past 24 hours or so um  the morning of the 27th yesterday you  had Russian missile strikes targeting  um Power facilities in the key region in  the center of the country and 